      "closure_rationale": "J1-J8 require exact invocation-context, same-thread live destination, variably modified scope and changed automatic-local reasoning. Only defined switch/equality/not placements execute: zero maps to one, volatile local7 and external effects11/19/23 persist across legal jumps. Nested changed context lives outside the actual er_run function containing setjmp. Draft N1570 clauses are inspected and not relabeled published C17/C23; invalid examples are never execution goldens. The actual bounded er_frame cleanup protocol composes unchanged ow_defer/ow_finish and the T66 typed counting allocator. A nested bridge drains only OW_ALWAYS entries; acquired-but-unregistered resources release directly before raising. The outer owner stays live through inner cleanup, then outer continuation registers a final owner. All owners drain before report publication; exact inner result and converted outer stage remain separate. Six compiler profiles execute5anchors,9compiled controls and5compiling-stub rejections. Original stack matrices cover0..5registration attempts, all8raised codes, normal return, cuts and capacity; the independent2160case owned-set oracle checks allocation attempts, cleanup order/masks, inner/outer results, finite publication headroom and unchanged invalid output. Actual ER_MUTANT11/12 and OW_MUTANT12 are separately rejected. Defined specimen runs in6compiler/mode combinations; static imports, stack/object/build observations and13cost dimensions remain bounded. The delayed nested-frame adapter performs actual third-resource allocation failure, failures before/after registration, and inner-to-outer cause conversion without disturbing outer cleanup order. Three successful inner acquisition effects can survive a converted error even though all five owners drain. This supplies author support after actual cleanup.scope PR-T66-02 and allocator PR-T66-09, without a reverse early prerequisite edge. Nonfailing cleanup and synchronous callbacks remain explicit; arbitrary external effects, fallible-close recovery and independent delayed learner assessment are separate. Bounded author support only."
